Rewrite: skip the intermediate ArrayList and the copy loop by writing straight into the result array.

`svalue.split(",")` has a fast path for single-char delimiters, but it still allocates an ArrayList and then an array. The intermediate `headers` list adds another copy. I write directly into the final array: `result[0]` is the name and `result[1..]` are the trimmed values.

Edge case: `"".split(",")` returns `[""]`, one element, so an empty svalue gives one trimmed empty string. `splitMultipartHeaderValues` returns at least one element, and `values.toArray` is unchanged.

The `values.length` array holds the split values. The `split` semantics (trailing empty strings removed) stay the same because I still call `split`. I keep the calls to `findNonWhitespace` and `findEndOfString` as they are.

