Each iteration called `getContainerAtIndex(i)` twice. For the mapped (immutable) implementation that call can create a container object, so the rewrite calls it once per iteration. The loop bound is also read once instead of on every pass. For non-run containers the original used `getCardinality(i)`, which on mapped arrays reads the stored cardinality, so I kept that call unchanged. `getCardinality(i)` is not called for run containers, which matches the original.

The original reads `highLowContainer` as a field. I kept that and did not assume its type beyond the methods already used.

