text:
The one real cost here is `lvProducerIndex()`, a volatile read. Only the single producer thread ever writes `producerIndex`, so `lpProducerIndex()`, a plain read, returns the same value and is cheaper. The sibling methods `relaxedOffer` and `fill` already use it this way. On x86 the volatile load costs little, but the plain read also lets the JIT optimize more freely. I made that one change and left the rest alone.

The spin-wait loop must keep its volatile loads, so it stays as is.

The change relies on the single-producer contract. It is only valid if `offer` is never called from more than one thread at a time.

